    <string name="settings_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_headline">No account, no ads, no tracking.</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body">Passo has no internet permission at all, so it cannot send your steps, your profile or your settings anywhere: they stay on the phone, unless you export them to a file yourself. Android’s own backup, if you turned it on, keeps a copy in your Google account, encrypted with your screen lock, to bring them to a new phone.</string>

